PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":2,"theme":"Helping Others","essential_question":"How can young people make their community better?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1","title":"I'll Bring the Bags! will for Offers, Promises and Predictions","objectives":["Students will be able to use will + base verb for offers, promises and quick decisions.","Students will be able to make predictions with I think … will / won't.","I can offer help: \"I'll carry that for you.\"","I can make a promise and a prediction with will and won't."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام will + الفعل الأصلي للعروض والوعود والقرارات السريعة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التوقع باستخدام I think … will / won't.","أستطيع أن أعرض المساعدة: I'll carry that for you.","أستطيع أن أقدّم وعدًا وتوقعًا باستخدام will وwon't."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"volunteer","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","definition":"a person who works for free to help others; to do this","arabic":"متطوع / يتطوع","example":"My brother volunteers at the hospital on weekends.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"community","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈmjunəti/","definition":"the people who live in one area","arabic":"مجتمع","example":"Our community built a new park.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"charity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɛrɪti/","definition":"an organization that helps people in need","arabic":"جمعية خيرية","example":"The charity gives food to poor families.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"donate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdoʊˌneɪt/","definition":"to give money or things to help others","arabic":"يتبرع","example":"We donated our old clothes.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use will ('ll) + base verb for: offers (I'll help you), promises (I'll call you), decisions we make now (It's cold – I'll close the window) and predictions or opinions about the future (I think it will rain).\nNegative: won't (= will not): I won't forget. Questions: Will you help me? – Yes, I will. / No, I won't.\nwill is the same for all subjects – no -s, no to: She will help (NOT she wills / she will to help).\noffer: I'll carry it for you.\npromise: I won't tell anyone. / I'll be on time.\ndecision now: The phone is ringing – I'll answer it.\nprediction/opinion: I think / Maybe / Probably + will","examples":["That box looks heavy. I'll carry it for you.","I'll call you when I get home – I promise.","I think our team will win tomorrow.","Don't worry. I won't forget your book.","Will you help me with this poster?","The bus is late. I'll walk to school.","In the future, people will use more solar energy.","Grandma won't like loud music."],"common_errors":["✗ I will to help you. → ✓ I will help you. (No to after will.)","✗ She wills come tomorrow. → ✓ She will come tomorrow. (will never takes -s.)","✗ I help you with your bags. (offer) → ✓ I'll help you with your bags. (Offers use will.)","✗ I don't will forget. → ✓ I won't forget. (will not → won't.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم will (أو 'll) + الفعل الأصلي للعرض (I'll help you) والوعد (I'll call you) والقرار اللحظي والتوقع (I think it will rain).\nالنفي: won't = will not، والسؤال: Will you help me?\nwill لا تتغير مع الضمائر ولا نضع بعدها to: She will help."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I'll Bring the Bags! will for Offers, Promises and Predictions”. Let’s learn will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U2-LS1 | I'll Bring the Bags! will for Offers, Promises and Predictions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The Park Clean-Up”: Next Saturday, our school is going to clean up the park near Al-Noor Mosque. Mr. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Next Saturday, our school is going to clean up the park near Al-Noor Mosque. Mr.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use will ('ll) + base verb for: offers (I'll help you), promises (I'll call you), decisions we make now (It's cold – I'll close the window) and predictions or opinions about the future (I think it will rain). Negative: won't (= will not): I won't forget. Questions: Will you help me? – Yes, I will. / No, I won't.","on_screen":"offer: I'll carry it for you. • promise: I won't tell anyone. / I'll be on time. • decision now: The phone is ringing – I'll answer it.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. That box looks heavy. I'll carry it for you. I'll call you when I get home – I promise. I think our team will win tomorrow.","on_screen":"That box looks heavy. I'll carry it for you. / I'll call you when I get home – I promise. / I think our team will win tomorrow.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I will to help you.” That’s not right. We say: “I will help you.” No to after will.","on_screen":"✗ I will to help you.   ✓ I will help you.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"That box looks heavy. I'll carry it.\" Is this an offer or a plan from last week? … Think! … An offer – decided now. Great job! Now you can say: I can offer help: \"I'll carry that for you.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can offer help: \"I'll carry that for you.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم will (أو 'll) + الفعل الأصلي للعرض (I'll help you) والوعد (I'll call you) والقرار اللحظي والتوقع (I think it will rain).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I will to help you. — الصحيح: I will help you.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعرض المساعدة: I'll carry that for you."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Park Clean-Up","body":"Next Saturday, our school is going to clean up the park near Al-Noor Mosque. Mr. Khalid asked, \"Who will help?\"\nEveryone raised a hand. \"I'll bring trash bags,\" said Omar. \"I'll carry the water,\" said Yusuf.\nAdam promised, \"I won't be late this time!\"\nMr. Khalid smiled. \"Thank you, boys. It will be hot, so wear hats. I think the park will look beautiful after our work.\"\nYusuf's father is a gardener. \"Will he help us plant trees?\" asked Omar.\n\"I'll ask him tonight,\" Yusuf answered.\nEveryone was excited to help the community.","word_count":93,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Your bags look heavy. I ___ carry one for you.","options":["carrying","'ll","will to","am going"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."},{"q":"I promise I ___ forget your birthday.","options":["won't","will not to","am not","don't"],"answer":"won't","explanation":"Promise: I'll / I won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الوعد بـ will أو won't."},{"q":"I think it ___ rain tomorrow.","options":["will","is","will to","wills"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"She will ___ us at the park.","options":["meeting","meets","meet","to meet"],"answer":"meet","explanation":"will + base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"will + الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"It's dark in here. I ___ turn on the light.","options":["am going to","will to","'ll","turning"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Decision at the moment of speaking → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي ← will."},{"q":"___ you help me with my homework?","options":["Are","Shall you","Do","Will"],"answer":"Will","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make offers or promises. Use I'll or I won't.","items":[{"q":"Your friend is thirsty. (get some water)  (offer)","options":[],"answer":"I'll get you some water.","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."},{"q":"Your mom asks you to be home early. (not / be late)  (promise)","options":[],"answer":"I won't be late.","explanation":"Promise: I'll / I won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الوعد بـ will أو won't."},{"q":"Your teacher drops her books. (pick them up)  (offer)","options":[],"answer":"I'll pick them up.","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write will or won't. Word bank: won't, will","items":[{"q":"Don't worry about the test. I'm sure you ______ do well.","options":[],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"My grandpa ______ eat sweets. He's careful about sugar.","options":[],"answer":"won't","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"I ______ call you after dinner. I promise!","options":[],"answer":"will","explanation":"Promise: I'll / I won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الوعد بـ will أو won't."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Respond with will.","items":[{"q":"Your little brother can't reach the book. You say: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'll get it for you.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your neighbor's car won't start. You say: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'll call my dad to help.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your friend is sad about his test. You promise: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'll help you study next time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will the weather be like tomorrow?","options":[],"answer":"I think it will be sunny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you think your town will look like in 2050?","options":[],"answer":"I think there will be more trees and electric cars.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Helping promises.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 promises to help at home this week.","options":[],"answer":"I'll make my bed every day. I'll help Mom in the kitchen. I won't leave my toys on the floor.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 predictions about your school in 10 years.","options":[],"answer":"There will be more computers. Students won't carry heavy books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a short dialogue (4 lines) with an offer and a thank you.","options":[],"answer":"A: Your bag is heavy. I'll carry it. B: Thank you! A: You're welcome. B: I'll help you next time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions.","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"I'll help"},{"label":"I'll carry"},{"label":"I won't forget"},{"label":"It will rain"},{"label":"Will you…?"},{"label":"I think … will"},{"label":"I promise I'll…"},{"label":"Shall I…?"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The baby is crying. I ___ check on him.","options":["am going to","'ll","will to","checking"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Decision at the moment of speaking → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي ← will."},{"q":"","options":["I won't tell anyone your secret.","I will not to tell anyone your secret.","I won't tells anyone your secret.","I don't will tell anyone your secret."],"answer":"I won't tell anyone your secret.","explanation":"will not = won't.","explanation_ar":"won't تعني will not."},{"q":"Maybe the new mall ___ open next year.","options":["is will","wills","will","will to"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"","options":["My dad will drives us to the park.","My dad will to drive us to the park.","My dad wills drive us to the park.","My dad will drive us to the park."],"answer":"My dad will drive us to the park.","explanation":"will + base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"will + الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"I'm hungry. – ___ make you a sandwich.","options":["I'd going to","I'll","I'm","I will to"],"answer":"I'll","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."},{"q":"Will Saad come to the clean-up? – Yes, he ___.","options":["is","wills","will","does"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"","options":["Don't worry, I'll help you.","Don't worry, I help you will.","Don't worry, I'll helping you.","Don't worry, I'll to help you."],"answer":"Don't worry, I'll help you.","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."},{"q":"I think people ___ live on Mars one day.","options":["wills","will to","will","are will"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"I promise I ___ clean my room.","options":["going","will","do","am"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Promise: I'll / I won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الوعد بـ will أو won't."},{"q":"","options":["It willn't be cold tomorrow.","It doesn't will be cold tomorrow.","It won't is cold tomorrow.","It won't be cold tomorrow."],"answer":"It won't be cold tomorrow.","explanation":"will not = won't.","explanation_ar":"won't تعني will not."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Mr. Khalid in class holding a flyer for a park clean-up while boys raise their hands to volunteer, one holding trash bags and one holding water bottles. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Mr. Khalid in class holding a flyer for a park clean-up while boys raise their hands to volunteer, one holding trash bags and one holding water bottles"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows volunteer (a person who works for free to help others; to do this); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing volunteer: a person who works for free to help others; to do this"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows community (the people who live in one area); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing community: the people who live in one area"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows charity (an organization that helps people in need); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing charity: an organization that helps people in need"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows donate (to give money or things to help others); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing donate: to give money or things to help others"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W01","script":"volunteer. volunteer. My brother volunteers at the hospital on weekends.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W02","script":"community. community. Our community built a new park.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W03","script":"charity. charity. The charity gives food to poor families.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-W04","script":"donate. donate. We donated our old clothes.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Next Saturday, our school is going to clean up the park near Al-Noor Mosque. Mr. Khalid asked, \"Who will help?\" Everyone raised a hand. \"I'll bring trash bags,\" said Omar. \"I'll carry the water,\" said Yusuf. Adam promised, \"I won't be late this time!\" Mr. Khalid smiled. \"Thank you, boys. It will be hot, so wear hats. I think the park will look beautiful after our work.\" Yusuf's father is a gardener. \"Will he help us plant trees?\" asked Omar. \"I'll ask him tonight,\" Yusuf answered. Everyone was excited to help the community.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I'll Bring the Bags! will for Offers, Promises and Predictions”. Let’s learn will / won't for offers, promises, decisions and predictions together. Listen to the start of “The Park Clean-Up”: Next Saturday, our school is going to clean up the park near Al-Noor Mosque. Mr. Look at the green words. We use will ('ll) + base verb for: offers (I'll help you), promises (I'll call you), decisions we make now (It's cold – I'll close the window) and predictions or opinions about the future (I think it will rain). Negative: won't (= will not): I won't forget. Questions: Will you help me? – Yes, I will. / No, I won't. Here are some examples. That box looks heavy. I'll carry it for you. I'll call you when I get home – I promise. I think our team will win tomorrow. Be careful! Some learners say: “I will to help you.” That’s not right. We say: “I will help you.” No to after will. Quick check: \"That box looks heavy. I'll carry it.\" Is this an offer or a plan from last week? … Think! … An offer – decided now. Great job! Now you can say: I can offer help: \"I'll carry that for you.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2","title":"Will or Going to?","objectives":["Students will be able to use going to for plans made before and will for decisions made now.","Students will be able to choose will for opinions and going to for predictions with evidence.","I can say \"I'm going to visit Grandma – it's my plan\" and \"OK, I'll come too!\"","I can choose will or going to for predictions."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام going to للخطط السابقة وwill للقرارات اللحظية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار will للآراء وgoing to للتوقعات المبنية على دليل.","أستطيع أن أقول I'm going to visit Grandma وOK, I'll come too!","أستطيع أن أختار will أو going to للتوقعات."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"neighbor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈneɪbɚ/","definition":"a person who lives near you","arabic":"جار","example":"Our neighbor brings us dates from his farm.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"elderly","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɛldɚli/","definition":"old (a polite word)","arabic":"كبار السن / مُسن","example":"We visited elderly people at the care home.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"recycle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"to use something again or make it into something new","arabic":"يعيد التدوير","example":"We recycle plastic bottles at school.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"clean up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/klin ʌp/","definition":"to make a place clean and tidy","arabic":"ينظّف (مكانًا)","example":"Let's clean up the beach together.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Plan (decided before) → be going to: I'm going to volunteer at the charity on Saturday (I already decided).\nDecision now (at the moment of speaking) → will: \"We need more volunteers.\" – \"OK, I'll come!\"\nPrediction with evidence (we can see it) → be going to: Look at those clouds! It's going to rain. Opinion or belief → will: I think it will rain tomorrow.","examples":["I'm going to visit my grandparents this weekend. It's all planned.","\"I'm thirsty.\" – \"I'll get you some water.\"","Look at that car! It's going to crash into the wall!","I think robots will do many jobs in the future.","We're going to donate our old toys to the charity.","\"Can someone help me?\" – \"Sure, I'll help.\"","My sister is going to start university in September.","Don't worry, the test won't be difficult."],"common_errors":["✗ \"The door is open.\" – \"I'm going to close it.\" (decided now) → ✓ \"I'll close it.\" (Decision now → will.)","✗ Look at those clouds! It will rain. → ✓ Look at those clouds! It's going to rain. (Evidence now → going to.)","✗ Next week I will visit my uncle. I bought the tickets. → ✓ Next week I'm going to visit my uncle. (A fixed plan → going to.)"],"arabic":"going to للخطط التي قررناها سابقًا، وwill للقرار في لحظة الكلام.\nللتوقع بدليل نراه الآن نستخدم going to (Look! It's going to rain)، وللرأي نستخدم will (I think it will rain).\nالعروض والوعود دائمًا بـ will."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Will or Going to?”. Let’s learn will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U2-LS2 | Will or Going to?","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: We're going to collect books next week. • \"The phone's ringing.\" – \"I'll get it.\" I'm not going to buy it. • I won't buy it. Are you going to help? • Will you help?","on_screen":"We're going to collect books next week. • \"The phone's ringing.\" – \"I'll get it.\" | I'm not going to buy it. • I won't buy it. | Are you going to help? • Will you help?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Plan (decided before) → be going to: I'm going to volunteer at the charity on Saturday (I already decided). Decision now (at the moment of speaking) → will: \"We need more volunteers.\" – \"OK, I'll come!\"","on_screen":"will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I'm going to visit my grandparents this weekend. It's all planned. \"I'm thirsty.\" – \"I'll get you some water.\" Look at that car! It's going to crash into the wall!","on_screen":"I'm going to visit my grandparents this weekend. It's all planned. / \"I'm thirsty.\" – \"I'll get you some water.\" / Look at that car! It's going to crash into the wall!","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “\"The door is open.\" – \"I'm going to close it.\" (decided now).” That’s not right. We say: “\"I'll close it.\".” Decision now → will.","on_screen":"✗ \"The door is open.\" – \"I'm going to close it.\" (decided now)   ✓ \"I'll close it.\"","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I've bought the tickets. I'm going to fly to Riyadh.\" Is this a plan or a decision now? … Think! … A plan – going to. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I'm going to visit Grandma – it's my plan\" and \"OK, I'll come too!\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I'm going to visit Grandma – it's my plan\" and \"OK, I'll come too!\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","going to للخطط التي قررناها سابقًا، وwill للقرار في لحظة الكلام.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: \"The door is open.\" – \"I'm going to close it.\" (decided now) — الصحيح: \"I'll close it.\"","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I'm going to visit Grandma وOK, I'll come too!"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"\"We need someone to carry the chairs.\" – \"OK, I ___ do it.\"","options":["'ll","going to","will to","'m going to"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"I ___ volunteer at the hospital next month. I signed up last week.","options":["going","'m going to","will to","'ll"],"answer":"'m going to","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"Look at the sky! It ___ rain.","options":["going","will to","wills","'s going to"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التوقع بدليل ← going to."},{"q":"I think the new library ___ be popular.","options":["is going","going","wills","will"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction as an opinion (I think) → will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع كرأي ← will."},{"q":"\"I forgot my pencil.\" – \"Don't worry, I ___ lend you one.\"","options":["'ll","'m going to","lend","going to"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"We ___ paint the school wall on Saturday. Everything is ready.","options":["'ll to","will to","'re going to","going"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write will or going to. Word bank: will, is going to, are going to","items":[{"q":"A: The phone is ringing. B: I ______ answer it.","options":[],"answer":"will","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"We ______ collect old books next week. We've already made posters.","options":[],"answer":"are going to","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"Watch out! That glass ______ fall!","options":[],"answer":"is going to","explanation":"Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التوقع بدليل ← going to."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"\"It's cold in here.\" – \"I'm going to close the window.\"","options":[],"answer":"\"It's cold in here.\" – \"I'll close the window.\"","explanation":"I'm going to close → I'll close. A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: I'm going to close → I'll close. القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"Look at that boy on the bike! He will fall!","options":[],"answer":"Look at that boy on the bike! He is going to fall!","explanation":"will → is going to. Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will → is going to. التوقع بدليل ← going to."},{"q":"I bought the paint yesterday. I will paint my room tomorrow.","options":[],"answer":"I bought the paint yesterday. I am going to paint my room tomorrow.","explanation":"will → am going to. A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will → am going to. الخطة السابقة ← going to."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer with will or going to.","items":[{"q":"What are you going to do this weekend? (a plan)","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to visit my cousins.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your friend's bag is open and his books are falling. What do you say?","options":[],"answer":"Your books are going to fall!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Your teacher asks for a helper. What do you say?","options":[],"answer":"I'll help!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do you think will happen in your town in ten years?","options":[],"answer":"I think there will be a metro.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What are you going to be when you grow up?","options":[],"answer":"I'm going to be a pilot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Plan a charity day.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 plans your class has already made with going to.","options":[],"answer":"We're going to sell cookies. We're going to collect clothes. We're going to give the money to a charity.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 offers classmates make in the meeting with I'll.","options":[],"answer":"I'll make posters. I'll bring tables. I'll count the money.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one prediction (opinion) about the day with will.","options":[],"answer":"I think many parents will come.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"offer / carry the bags"},{"cue":"promise / not be late"},{"cue":"prediction / the park / look great"},{"cue":"offer / open the door"},{"cue":"promise / call you tonight"},{"cue":"prediction / it / rain tomorrow"},{"cue":"decision now / take the bus"},{"cue":"offer / help with homework"},{"cue":"prediction / people / love the garden"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"\"There's no bread.\" – \"I ___ buy some on my way home.\"","options":["'ll","'m going to have","going to","buying"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"My brother ___ study medicine. He decided last year.","options":["is going to","going","wills","will to"],"answer":"is going to","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"Be careful! The cat ___ jump on the table!","options":["going","'s going to","will to","wills"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التوقع بدليل ← going to."},{"q":"I'm sure you ___ love this book.","options":["'re going to be","going to","will to","'ll"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Prediction as an opinion (I think) → will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع كرأي ← will."},{"q":"","options":["\"I can't open this jar.\" – \"I'll help you.\"","\"I can't open this jar.\" – \"I help you will.\"","\"I can't open this jar.\" – \"I'll to help you.\"","\"I can't open this jar.\" – \"I'm going to help you yesterday.\""],"answer":"\"I can't open this jar.\" – \"I'll help you.\"","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"","options":["We'll visit the elderly care home on Sunday, it's on our calendar going.","We going to visit the elderly care home on Sunday.","We're going visit the elderly care home on Sunday.","We're going to visit the elderly care home on Sunday. It's on our calendar."],"answer":"We're going to visit the elderly care home on Sunday. It's on our calendar.","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"Look at the score: 5–0! Our team ___ win!","options":["going","wills","'s going to","will to"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التوقع بدليل ← going to."},{"q":"Probably people ___ drive flying cars one day.","options":["wills","are going","will","going"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction as an opinion (I think) → will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع كرأي ← will."},{"q":"Which one is a decision made now?","options":["\"I'm going to open a shop next year.\"","\"It's hot. I'll open the window.\"","\"Look! It's going to rain.\"","\"We're going to travel in June.\""],"answer":"\"It's hot. I'll open the window.\"","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"Which one is a plan?","options":["\"I'll get it!\"","\"I think it will snow.\"","\"OK, I'll join you!\"","\"I'm going to join the robotics club next term.\""],"answer":"\"I'm going to join the robotics club next term.\"","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two speech bubbles: Yusuf with a calendar saying his plan for Saturday, and Omar suddenly deciding to join him; a dark cloud above a girl with an umbrella. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two speech bubbles: Yusuf with a calendar saying his plan for Saturday, and Omar suddenly deciding to join him; a dark cloud above a girl with an umbrella"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Helping Others”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of will vs be going to (decision now vs plan"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows neighbor (a person who lives near you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing neighbor: a person who lives near you"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows elderly (old (a polite word)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing elderly: old (a polite word)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows recycle (to use something again or make it into something new); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing recycle: to use something again or make it into something new"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows clean up (to make a place clean and tidy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing clean up: to make a place clean and tidy"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W01","script":"neighbor. neighbor. Our neighbor brings us dates from his farm.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W02","script":"elderly. elderly. We visited elderly people at the care home.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W03","script":"recycle. recycle. We recycle plastic bottles at school.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-W04","script":"clean up. clean up. Let's clean up the beach together.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Will or Going to?”. Let’s learn will vs be going to (decision now vs plan; opinion vs evidence) together. Remember these patterns: We're going to collect books next week. • \"The phone's ringing.\" – \"I'll get it.\" I'm not going to buy it. • I won't buy it. Are you going to help? • Will you help? Plan (decided before) → be going to: I'm going to volunteer at the charity on Saturday (I already decided). Decision now (at the moment of speaking) → will: \"We need more volunteers.\" – \"OK, I'll come!\" Here are some examples. I'm going to visit my grandparents this weekend. It's all planned. \"I'm thirsty.\" – \"I'll get you some water.\" Look at that car! It's going to crash into the wall! Be careful! Some learners say: “\"The door is open.\" – \"I'm going to close it.\" (decided now).” That’s not right. We say: “\"I'll close it.\".” Decision now → will. Quick check: \"I've bought the tickets. I'm going to fly to Riyadh.\" Is this a plan or a decision now? … Think! … A plan – going to. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I'm going to visit Grandma – it's my plan\" and \"OK, I'll come too!\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3","title":"Volunteers and Neighbors: Community Words with re- and un-","objectives":["Students will be able to use words about volunteering and community.","Students will be able to understand and form words with re- (again) and un- (not).","I can talk about helping my community.","I can explain words like \"reuse\" and \"unkind\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات التطوع والمجتمع.","سيتمكن الطلاب من فهم وتكوين كلمات بالبادئتين re- (مرة أخرى) وun- (عدم).","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن مساعدة مجتمعي.","أستطيع أن أشرح كلمات مثل reuse وunkind."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"collect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkt/","definition":"to bring things together from different places","arabic":"يجمع","example":"The students collected books for the library.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"kind","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kaɪnd/","definition":"friendly and helpful to others","arabic":"لطيف / طيب","example":"It was kind of you to help me.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"generous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʒɛnɚəs/","definition":"happy to give money, time or things","arabic":"كريم","example":"My uncle is very generous to his neighbors.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"share","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ʃɛr/","definition":"to give part of something to others","arabic":"يشارك / يقتسم","example":"Please share your crayons with Ali.","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W04"},{"word":"help out","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/hɛlp aʊt/","definition":"to help someone, especially for a short time","arabic":"يُساعد / يمدّ يد العون","example":"Can you help out at the school fair?","image_id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Community words: volunteer (work for free), charity, donate, neighbor, elderly, generous, share, collect, clean up, help out.\nThe prefix re- means again: reuse = use again, refill = fill again, rebuild = build again, recycle = use materials again.\nThe prefix un- means not or the opposite: unkind = not kind, unhappy, unfair, unsafe, untidy.\nCollocations/phrases: re- = again: reuse • refill • rebuild • rewrite • retell • recycle | un- = not: unkind • unhappy • unfair • unsafe • untidy • unhealthy | donate money/clothes • volunteer at a charity • help out a neighbor • clean up the beach • share food","examples":["My cousin volunteers at a food bank.","We donated blankets to families in need.","Let's reuse these jars for our art project.","Please refill your water bottle at the fountain.","It's unkind to laugh at other people.","Playing near the road is unsafe.","Our neighbor is generous – he shares his dates with everyone.","The students cleaned up the beach in Jeddah."],"common_errors":["✗ I will give a donate. → ✓ I will donate / make a donation. (donate is a verb.)","✗ It is not kind to shout. → It is unkindly to shout. → ✓ It is unkind to shout. (Use the adjective unkind.)","✗ We use again the bottles. → ✓ We reuse the bottles. (re- = again.)","✗ The old people in the home → ✓ The elderly people in the home (elderly is more polite.)"],"arabic":"كلمات المجتمع: volunteer (متطوع) وcharity (جمعية خيرية) وdonate (يتبرع) وneighbor (جار) وgenerous (كريم).\nالبادئة re تعني «مرة أخرى»: reuse = يستخدم مرة أخرى، refill = يعيد التعبئة.\nالبادئة un تعني «غير / عدم»: unkind = غير لطيف، unsafe = غير آمن.\nكلمة elderly أكثر تهذيبًا من old للحديث عن كبار السن."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Volunteers and Neighbors: Community Words with re- and un-”. Let’s learn community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U2-LS3 | Volunteers and Neighbors: Community Words with re- and un-","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. collect: to bring things together from different places. kind: friendly and helpful to others. generous: happy to give money, time or things.","on_screen":"collect | kind | generous","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Community words: volunteer (work for free), charity, donate, neighbor, elderly, generous, share, collect, clean up, help out. The prefix re- means again: reuse = use again, refill = fill again, rebuild = build again, recycle = use materials again.","on_screen":"community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My cousin volunteers at a food bank. We donated blankets to families in need. Let's reuse these jars for our art project.","on_screen":"My cousin volunteers at a food bank. / We donated blankets to families in need. / Let's reuse these jars for our art project.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I will give a donate.” That’s not right. We say: “I will donate / make a donation.” donate is a verb.","on_screen":"✗ I will give a donate.   ✓ I will donate / make a donation.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What does \"rebuild\" mean? … Think! … Build again. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about helping my community.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about helping my community.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كلمات المجتمع: volunteer (متطوع) وcharity (جمعية خيرية) وdonate (يتبرع) وneighbor (جار) وgenerous (كريم).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I will give a donate. — الصحيح: I will donate / make a donation.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن مساعدة مجتمعي."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"re + use = ___ (use again)","options":["unuse","useless","reuse","reused again"],"answer":"reuse","explanation":"re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"Laughing at people is ___.","options":["kindness","rekind","unkind","kindly"],"answer":"unkind","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"People who work for free to help are ___.","options":["charities","volunteers","neighbors","donors'"],"answer":"volunteers","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"We ___ our old clothes to the charity.","options":["collected from","recycled","shared out","donated"],"answer":"donated","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"The house next to ours is our ___ house.","options":["neighbor's","elderly's","charity's","volunteer's"],"answer":"neighbor's","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"Please ___ your bottle at the water cooler.","options":["unfill","refill","fill again re","overfill"],"answer":"refill","explanation":"re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to the meaning.","items":[{"q":"unfair","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"not fair","explanation":"unfair → not fair. re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"rewrite","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"write again","explanation":"rewrite → write again. re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"generous","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"happy to give","explanation":"generous → happy to give. re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"unsafe","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"not safe","explanation":"unsafe → not safe. re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"rebuild","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"build again","explanation":"rebuild → build again. re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"elderly","options":["old (polite)","build again","write again","not safe","happy to give","not fair"],"answer":"old (polite)","explanation":"elderly → old (polite). re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about helping.","items":[{"q":"One way I help my neighbors is ___.","options":[],"answer":"One way I help my neighbors is carrying their shopping.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I can reuse at home is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Something I can reuse at home is a glass jar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A charity I know is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A charity I know is a food bank in our city.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"It's unkind to ___.","options":[],"answer":"It's unkind to ignore a new student.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I can donate ___.","options":[],"answer":"I can donate my old books.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a \"Kindness Poster\".","items":[{"q":"Write 4 rules for a kind classroom with un- words.","options":[],"answer":"Don't be unkind. Don't leave the room untidy. Don't be unfair in games. Don't do anything unsafe.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 re- words and use them in sentences.","options":[],"answer":"We reuse paper. I refill my bottle. I rewrite my story.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about a generous person you know.","options":[],"answer":"My grandpa is generous – he helps poor families.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"volunteer","match":"a person who works for free to help others; to do this","arabic":"متطوع / يتطوع"},{"word":"community","match":"the people who live in one area","arabic":"مجتمع"},{"word":"charity","match":"an organization that helps people in need","arabic":"جمعية خيرية"},{"word":"donate","match":"to give money or things to help others","arabic":"يتبرع"},{"word":"neighbor","match":"a person who lives near you","arabic":"جار"},{"word":"elderly","match":"old (a polite word)","arabic":"كبار السن / مُسن"},{"word":"recycle","match":"to use something again or make it into something new","arabic":"يعيد التدوير"},{"word":"clean up","match":"to make a place clean and tidy","arabic":"ينظّف (مكانًا)"},{"word":"collect","match":"to bring things together from different places","arabic":"يجمع"},{"word":"kind","match":"friendly and helpful to others","arabic":"لطيف / طيب"},{"word":"generous","match":"happy to give money, time or things","arabic":"كريم"},{"word":"share","match":"to give part of something to others","arabic":"يشارك / يقتسم"},{"word":"help out","match":"to help someone, especially for a short time","arabic":"يُساعد / يمدّ يد العون"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"un + happy = ___","options":["happyun","dishappy","rehappy","unhappy"],"answer":"unhappy","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"re + build = ___","options":["unbuild","rebuild","overbuild","buildre"],"answer":"rebuild","explanation":"re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"A person who lives next to you is your ___.","options":["volunteer","charity","neighbor","donor"],"answer":"neighbor","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"Our class ___ 200 books for the library.","options":["collected","volunteered","shared out","recycled"],"answer":"collected","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"A polite word for old people is ___.","options":["elderly","oldy","aged-up","olden"],"answer":"elderly","explanation":"elderly is a polite word for old people.","explanation_ar":"elderly كلمة مهذبة."},{"q":"It's ___ to play with matches.","options":["resafe","safely","unsafe","safety"],"answer":"unsafe","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"The ___ gives food to poor families.","options":["volunteer's","neighbor","charity","elderly"],"answer":"charity","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"Please ___ your story with neater handwriting.","options":["rewrite","write re","miswrite","unwrite"],"answer":"rewrite","explanation":"re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"My uncle gives a lot to others. He's very ___.","options":["unfair","generous","elderly","unkind"],"answer":"generous","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"Which word means \"not fair\"?","options":["fairly","fairness","refair","unfair"],"answer":"unfair","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A community center: volunteers sorting donated clothes, a recycling station with bins, a boy refilling water bottles, and an elderly man smiling as a girl helps him. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A community center: volunteers sorting donated clothes, a recycling station with bins, a boy refilling water bottles, and an elderly man smiling as a girl helps him"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows collect (to bring things together from different places); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing collect: to bring things together from different places"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows kind (friendly and helpful to others); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing kind: friendly and helpful to others"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows generous (happy to give money, time or things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing generous: happy to give money, time or things"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows share (to give part of something to others); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing share: to give part of something to others"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows help out (to help someone, especially for a short time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing help out: to help someone, especially for a short time"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W01","script":"collect. collect. The students collected books for the library.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W02","script":"kind. kind. It was kind of you to help me.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W03","script":"generous. generous. My uncle is very generous to his neighbors.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W04","script":"share. share. Please share your crayons with Ali.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-W05","script":"help out. help out. Can you help out at the school fair?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Volunteers and Neighbors: Community Words with re- and un-”. Let’s learn community and volunteering words; prefixes re- (again) and un- (not) together. Meet some new words. collect: to bring things together from different places. kind: friendly and helpful to others. generous: happy to give money, time or things. Community words: volunteer (work for free), charity, donate, neighbor, elderly, generous, share, collect, clean up, help out. The prefix re- means again: reuse = use again, refill = fill again, rebuild = build again, recycle = use materials again. Here are some examples. My cousin volunteers at a food bank. We donated blankets to families in need. Let's reuse these jars for our art project. Be careful! Some learners say: “I will give a donate.” That’s not right. We say: “I will donate / make a donation.” donate is a verb. Quick check: What does \"rebuild\" mean? … Think! … Build again. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about helping my community.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4","title":"First, Next, Finally: Commas after Introductory Words","objectives":["Students will be able to put a comma after introductory words like First, Finally and However.","Students will be able to use a comma after Yes, No and Well in answers.","I can write \"First, we collected the trash.\"","I can write \"Yes, I'll help.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع فاصلة بعد الكلمات الاستهلالية مثل First وFinally وHowever.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام فاصلة بعد Yes وNo وWell في الإجابات.","أستطيع أن أكتب First, we collected the trash.","أستطيع أن أكتب Yes, I'll help."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"volunteer","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","definition":"a person who works for free to help others; to do this","arabic":"متطوع / يتطوع","example":"My brother volunteers at the hospital on weekends.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"community","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈmjunəti/","definition":"the people who live in one area","arabic":"مجتمع","example":"Our community built a new park.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"charity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɛrɪti/","definition":"an organization that helps people in need","arabic":"جمعية خيرية","example":"The charity gives food to poor families.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"donate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdoʊˌneɪt/","definition":"to give money or things to help others","arabic":"يتبرع","example":"We donated our old clothes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"neighbor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈneɪbɚ/","definition":"a person who lives near you","arabic":"جار","example":"Our neighbor brings us dates from his farm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"elderly","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɛldɚli/","definition":"old (a polite word)","arabic":"كبار السن / مُسن","example":"We visited elderly people at the care home.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"When a sentence starts with an introductory word, put a comma after it: First, we met at the park. Finally, we planted the trees.\nCommon introductory words: First, Second, Next, Then, After that, Finally, However, Also, Luckily, Sadly.\nPut a comma after Yes, No and Well at the start of an answer: Yes, I will. No, thank you. Well, I'm not sure.\nSequence words at the start → comma: Next, …\nHowever / Also / Luckily at the start → comma: However, …\nYes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma: Yes, I can.\nDon't use a comma when the word is not at the start: We then cleaned the benches.","examples":["First, we put on our gloves.","Next, we picked up the plastic bottles.","After that, we sorted the trash into bins.","Finally, we planted ten small trees.","However, some people didn't come.","Yes, I'll help you with the boxes.","No, thank you. I'm fine.","Luckily, the weather was cool."],"common_errors":["✗ First we collected the bottles. → ✓ First, we collected the bottles. (Comma after the introductory word.)","✗ Yes I will. → ✓ Yes, I will. (Comma after Yes.)","✗ However the park was clean. → ✓ However, the park was clean. (Comma after However.)","✗ Finally, we, planted the trees. → ✓ Finally, we planted the trees. (Only one comma, after Finally.)"],"arabic":"عندما تبدأ الجملة بكلمة استهلالية مثل First أو Finally أو However نضع فاصلة بعدها.\nنضع فاصلة بعد Yes وNo وWell في بداية الإجابة: Yes, I will.\nلا نضع فواصل إضافية داخل الجملة بلا سبب."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “First, Next, Finally: Commas after Introductory Words”. Let’s learn commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U2-LS4 | First, Next, Finally: Commas after Introductory Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"When a sentence starts with an introductory word, put a comma after it: First, we met at the park. Finally, we planted the trees.","on_screen":"commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When a sentence starts with an introductory word, put a comma after it: First, we met at the park. Finally, we planted the trees. Common introductory words: First, Second, Next, Then, After that, Finally, However, Also, Luckily, Sadly.","on_screen":"Sequence words at the start → comma: Next, … • However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma: However, … • Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma: Yes, I can.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. First, we put on our gloves. Next, we picked up the plastic bottles. After that, we sorted the trash into bins.","on_screen":"First, we put on our gloves. / Next, we picked up the plastic bottles. / After that, we sorted the trash into bins.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “First we collected the bottles.” That’s not right. We say: “First, we collected the bottles.” Comma after the introductory word.","on_screen":"✗ First we collected the bottles.   ✓ First, we collected the bottles.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Where does the comma go in \"Luckily we found the keys\"? … Think! … After *Luckily*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"First, we collected the trash.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"First, we collected the trash.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","عندما تبدأ الجملة بكلمة استهلالية مثل First أو Finally أو However نضع فاصلة بعدها.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: First we collected the bottles. — الصحيح: First, we collected the bottles.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب First, we collected the trash."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Clean-Up Day (editing passage)","body":"First we met at the park at eight. Next we collected plastic bottles and bags. However some trash was under the bushes. After that we planted trees with Yusuf's father. Finally we took a group photo. Yes it was a great day!","word_count":42,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["First we, washed our hands.","First we washed, our hands.","First, we washed our hands.",", First we washed our hands."],"answer":"First, we washed our hands.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Yes, I'll come to the clean-up.","Yes, I'll, come to the clean-up.","Yes I'll, come to the clean-up.","Yes I'll come to the clean-up."],"answer":"Yes, I'll come to the clean-up.","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["However, the shop was closed.","However the shop, was closed.","However the shop was closed.","However, the shop, was closed."],"answer":"However, the shop was closed.","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Finally we thanked the volunteers.","Finally, we thanked, the volunteers.","Finally we, thanked the volunteers.","Finally, we thanked the volunteers."],"answer":"Finally, we thanked the volunteers.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["No thank, you. I'm not hungry.","No, thank you. I'm not hungry.","No thank you. I'm not hungry.","No, thank, you. I'm not hungry."],"answer":"No, thank you. I'm not hungry.","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Luckily nobody was hurt.","Luckily, nobody was hurt.","Luckily nobody, was hurt.","Luckily, nobody, was hurt."],"answer":"Luckily, nobody was hurt.","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add or remove a comma.","items":[{"q":"Next we painted the fence.","options":[],"answer":"Next, we painted the fence.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Well I'm not sure about that.","options":[],"answer":"Well, I'm not sure about that.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Also we collected old clothes.","options":[],"answer":"Also, we collected old clothes.","explanation":"(add) → ,. However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"After that we had lunch together.","options":[],"answer":"After that, we had lunch together.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We, then cleaned the benches.","options":[],"answer":"We then cleaned the benches.","explanation":", → (delete). Don't add extra commas.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). لا تضع فواصل زائدة."},{"q":"Sadly the rain stopped our game.","options":[],"answer":"Sadly, the rain stopped our game.","explanation":"(add) → ,. However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. However في البداية ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the volunteer report.","items":[{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"First we met at the park at eight.","options":[],"answer":"First, we met at the park at eight.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write a process.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 steps for making tea with First, Next, Then and Finally.","options":[],"answer":"First, boil the water. Next, put the tea in a cup. Then pour the water. Finally, add some sugar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Answer the question \"Will you help at the school fair?\" with Yes or No and a comma.","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I will.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence that starts with However.","options":[],"answer":"However, I can't come on Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"volunteer","clue":"a person who works for free to help others; to do this"},{"word":"community","clue":"the people who live in one area"},{"word":"charity","clue":"an organization that helps people in need"},{"word":"donate","clue":"to give money or things to help others"},{"word":"neighbor","clue":"a person who lives near you"},{"word":"generous","clue":"happy to give money, time or things"},{"word":"elderly","clue":"old (a polite word)"},{"word":"recycle","clue":"to use something again or make it into something new"},{"word":"collect","clue":"to bring things together from different places"},{"word":"kind","clue":"friendly and helpful to others"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Then we, sorted the trash into bins.","Then, we sorted, the trash into bins.","Then, we sorted the trash into bins.","Then we sorted the trash, into bins."],"answer":"Then, we sorted the trash into bins.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"Yes I can help you.\"","options":["after \"I\"","after \"Yes\"","after \"can\"","after \"help\""],"answer":"after \"Yes\"","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["However, we, finished on time.","However we finished on time.","However, we finished on time.","However we, finished on time."],"answer":"However, we finished on time.","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Well let's ask the teacher.","Well, let's, ask the teacher.","Well let's, ask the teacher.","Well, let's ask the teacher."],"answer":"Well, let's ask the teacher.","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["After that we, visited the elderly care home.","After, that we visited the elderly care home.","After that, we visited the elderly care home.","After that we visited the elderly care home."],"answer":"After that, we visited the elderly care home.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Spot the sentence that is missing a comma.","options":["Finally the volunteers went home.","The volunteers finally went home.","The volunteers went home.","We went home finally."],"answer":"Finally the volunteers went home.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We, then, cleaned the windows.","We then cleaned the windows.","We then, cleaned the windows.","We, then cleaned the windows."],"answer":"We then cleaned the windows.","explanation":"Don't add extra commas.","explanation_ar":"لا تضع فواصل زائدة."},{"q":"","options":["No, I, don't need any help.","No, I don't need any help.","No I don't, need any help.","No I don't need any help."],"answer":"No, I don't need any help.","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Luckily, the bus came on time.","Luckily the bus, came on time.","Luckily the bus came on time.","Luckily, the bus, came on time."],"answer":"Luckily, the bus came on time.","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Second we put, the books in boxes.","Second, we put, the books in boxes.","Second we put the books in boxes.","Second, we put the books in boxes."],"answer":"Second, we put the books in boxes.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Helping Others” that shows commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Helping Others” that shows commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “First, Next, Finally: Commas after Introductory Words”. Let’s learn commas after introductory words (First, Next, Then, Finally, However, Yes, No, Well) together. When a sentence starts with an introductory word, put a comma after it: First, we met at the park. Finally, we planted the trees. When a sentence starts with an introductory word, put a comma after it: First, we met at the park. Finally, we planted the trees. Common introductory words: First, Second, Next, Then, After that, Finally, However, Also, Luckily, Sadly. Here are some examples. First, we put on our gloves. Next, we picked up the plastic bottles. After that, we sorted the trash into bins. Be careful! Some learners say: “First we collected the bottles.” That’s not right. We say: “First, we collected the bottles.” Comma after the introductory word. Quick check: Where does the comma go in \"Luckily we found the keys\"? … Think! … After *Luckily*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"First, we collected the trash.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5","title":"Our Kindness Project: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to plan a class kindness project, making offers and predictions.","Students will be able to write a project plan with going to, will and sequence words with commas.","I can plan a kindness project with my team.","I can write our project plan."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التخطيط لمشروع لطف صفي مع تقديم العروض والتوقعات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة خطة مشروع باستخدام going to وwill وكلمات التسلسل مع الفواصل.","أستطيع أن أخطط لمشروع لطف مع فريقي.","أستطيع أن أكتب خطة مشروعنا."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"volunteer","pos":"noun / verb","ipa":"/ˌvɑlənˈtɪr/","definition":"a person who works for free to help others; to do this","arabic":"متطوع / يتطوع","example":"My brother volunteers at the hospital on weekends.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"community","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈmjunəti/","definition":"the people who live in one area","arabic":"مجتمع","example":"Our community built a new park.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"charity","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃɛrɪti/","definition":"an organization that helps people in need","arabic":"جمعية خيرية","example":"The charity gives food to poor families.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"donate","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈdoʊˌneɪt/","definition":"to give money or things to help others","arabic":"يتبرع","example":"We donated our old clothes.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"neighbor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈneɪbɚ/","definition":"a person who lives near you","arabic":"جار","example":"Our neighbor brings us dates from his farm.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"elderly","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɛldɚli/","definition":"old (a polite word)","arabic":"كبار السن / مُسن","example":"We visited elderly people at the care home.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"recycle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"to use something again or make it into something new","arabic":"يعيد التدوير","example":"We recycle plastic bottles at school.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"clean up","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/klin ʌp/","definition":"to make a place clean and tidy","arabic":"ينظّف (مكانًا)","example":"Let's clean up the beach together.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"collect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kəˈlɛkt/","definition":"to bring things together from different places","arabic":"يجمع","example":"The students collected books for the library.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kind","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kaɪnd/","definition":"friendly and helpful to others","arabic":"لطيف / طيب","example":"It was kind of you to help me.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"generous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʒɛnɚəs/","definition":"happy to give money, time or things","arabic":"كريم","example":"My uncle is very generous to his neighbors.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"share","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ʃɛr/","definition":"to give part of something to others","arabic":"يشارك / يقتسم","example":"Please share your crayons with Ali.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"help out","pos":"phrasal verb","ipa":"/hɛlp aʊt/","definition":"to help someone, especially for a short time","arabic":"يُساعد / يمدّ يد العون","example":"Can you help out at the school fair?","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 2: will (offers, promises, opinions), going to (plans, evidence), community words, re-/un- and commas after introductory words.\nA project plan says what you are going to do, who will help, and what you think will happen.\n✔ plans → We're going to…\n✔ offers/promises → I'll… / I won't…\n✔ opinions → I think … will…\n✔ First, Next, Finally + comma","examples":["We're going to clean the beach on Friday.","First, we're going to buy gloves.","I'll bring trash bags.","I promise I won't be late.","Next, we're going to sort the bottles to recycle them.","I think the beach will look wonderful.","However, we need more volunteers.","Finally, we're going to thank everyone."],"common_errors":["✗ First we will going to collect books. → ✓ First, we're going to collect books. (Plan → going to; comma after First.)","✗ \"Who can help?\" – \"I'm going to help!\" → ✓ \"I'll help!\" (Offer made now → will.)","✗ It is not fair → It is unfairly. → ✓ It is unfair. (Use the adjective with un-.)"],"arabic":"نراجع will وgoing to وكلمات المجتمع والبادئات re وun والفواصل بعد الكلمات الاستهلالية.\nخطة المشروع: ماذا سنفعل (going to)، ومَن سيساعد (I'll)، وماذا نتوقع (I think … will).\nتذكّر الفاصلة بعد First وNext وFinally."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Kindness Project: Language in Use”. Let’s learn will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U2-LS5 | Our Kindness Project: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Kindness meeting: in teams, choose a project (book drive, park clean-up, visiting the elderly). Each person makes an offer with \"I'll…\". The team agrees on 3 plans with \"We're going to…\" and makes one prediction with \"I think … will…\".","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 2: will (offers, promises, opinions), going to (plans, evidence), community words, re-/un- and commas after introductory words. A project plan says what you are going to do, who will help, and what you think will happen.","on_screen":"✔ plans → We're going to… • ✔ offers/promises → I'll… / I won't… • ✔ opinions → I think … will…","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We're going to clean the beach on Friday. First, we're going to buy gloves. I'll bring trash bags.","on_screen":"We're going to clean the beach on Friday. / First, we're going to buy gloves. / I'll bring trash bags.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “First we will going to collect books.” That’s not right. We say: “First, we're going to collect books.” Plan → going to; comma after First.","on_screen":"✗ First we will going to collect books.   ✓ First, we're going to collect books.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “\"Who can help?\" – \"I'm going to help!\"”? … Think! … It should be “\"I'll help!\"”. Great job! Now you can say: I can plan a kindness project with my team.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can plan a kindness project with my team.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع will وgoing to وكلمات المجتمع والبادئات re وun والفواصل بعد الكلمات الاستهلالية.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: First we will going to collect books. — الصحيح: First, we're going to collect books.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أخطط لمشروع لطف مع فريقي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Our Book Drive – Team 4B","body":"We're going to collect books for the children's hospital.\nFirst, we're going to put posters around the school.\nNext, we're going to put boxes in every classroom.\nOmar said, \"I'll collect the boxes every day,\" and Adam promised, \"I won't forget to count the books.\"\nFinally, we're going to reuse old cardboard to make bookmarks.\nI think the children will be very happy with their new books!","word_count":67,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the plan. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Team 4B is going to collect books for a hospital.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They're going to put posters around the school first.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam is going to collect the boxes every day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam promised not to forget to count the books.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"They're going to buy new cardboard for bookmarks.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The writer thinks the children will be happy.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Our Book Drive – Team 4B”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The team ___ collect books. They planned it last week.","options":["going","will to","wills","is going to"],"answer":"is going to","explanation":"Plan → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"\"Who can carry the boxes?\" – \"I ___ do it!\"","options":["going to","'m going to have","will to","'ll"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Offer, promise or opinion → will.","explanation_ar":"العرض أو الوعد أو الرأي ← will."},{"q":"They're going to ___ old cardboard to make bookmarks.","options":["unuse","overuse","reuse","useless"],"answer":"reuse","explanation":"re- = again; un- = not.","explanation_ar":"البادئات."},{"q":"","options":["Next, we're going to put boxes in every classroom.","Next, we're going to, put boxes in every classroom.","Next we're, going to put boxes in every classroom.","Next we're going to put boxes in every classroom."],"answer":"Next, we're going to put boxes in every classroom.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory word.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد الكلمة الاستهلالية."},{"q":"People who give books for free are ___.","options":["charities","donors","neighbors","elderlies"],"answer":"donors","explanation":"Community word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة المجتمع."},{"q":"I think the children ___ love the books.","options":["are going","will","wills","going"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Offer, promise or opinion → will.","explanation_ar":"العرض أو الوعد أو الرأي ← will."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Kindness meeting. Write what your team says.","items":[{"q":"Our project: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Our project is a park clean-up.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An offer from me: I'll ___.","options":[],"answer":"I'll bring gloves and trash bags.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An offer from a teammate: ___.","options":[],"answer":"Saad: \"I'll make the posters.\"","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Our plan: We're going to ___.","options":[],"answer":"We're going to meet at the park at eight.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A prediction: I think ___ will ___.","options":[],"answer":"I think the park will look much better.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your project plan.","items":[{"q":"Plan: project, 3 steps, 2 offers, 1 prediction.","options":[],"answer":"visit the elderly care home; make cards, buy flowers, visit on Thursday; Ali will bring dates, I'll read a story; they will be happy","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your team's plan in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"We're going to visit the elderly care home on Thursday. First, we're going to make cards. Next, we're going to buy flowers. Ali said, \"I'll bring dates.\" I'll read a story to them. Finally, we're going to sing a nasheed. I think they will be very happy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: going to for plans? will for offers? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"First we\" to \"First, we\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"volunteer","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"community","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"charity","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"donate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"neighbor","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"elderly","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"recycle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"clean up","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"collect","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"kind","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"generous","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"share","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"help out","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ visit the charity next Monday. It's on our calendar.","options":["'re going to","'ll to","going","wills"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"Plan → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"\"This box is heavy!\" – \"Wait, I ___ help you.\"","options":["'ll","helping","'m going to yesterday","going to"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Offer, promise or opinion → will.","explanation_ar":"العرض أو الوعد أو الرأي ← will."},{"q":"The opposite of \"safe\" is ___.","options":["safely","resafe","unsafe","dissafe"],"answer":"unsafe","explanation":"re- = again; un- = not.","explanation_ar":"البادئات."},{"q":"","options":["Finally we gave the books to the children.","Finally, we gave the books to the children.","Finally we, gave the books to the children.","Finally, we gave the books, to the children."],"answer":"Finally, we gave the books to the children.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory word.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد الكلمة الاستهلالية."},{"q":"A person who works for free to help others is a ___.","options":["donation","volunteer","neighbor","charity"],"answer":"volunteer","explanation":"Community word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة المجتمع."},{"q":"","options":["I promise I won't to forget the posters.","I promise I won't forgets the posters.","I promise I don't will forget the posters.","I promise I won't forget the posters."],"answer":"I promise I won't forget the posters.","explanation":"Offer, promise or opinion → will.","explanation_ar":"العرض أو الوعد أو الرأي ← will."},{"q":"Look! The volunteers ___ finish the wall soon. Only one part is left.","options":["going","will to","are going to","wills"],"answer":"are going to","explanation":"Plan → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة ← going to."},{"q":"","options":["Yes I'll, join your team.","Yes I'll join your team.","Yes, I'll join your team.","Yes, I'll, join your team."],"answer":"Yes, I'll join your team.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory word.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد الكلمة الاستهلالية."},{"q":"We ___ old paper for our art project.","options":["recycle","decycle","cycle again","uncycle"],"answer":"recycle","explanation":"re- = again; un- = not.","explanation_ar":"البادئات."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a project plan:","options":["First, we going to collect old clothes.","First we're going to, collect old clothes.","First we will going to collect old clothes.","First, we're going to collect old clothes."],"answer":"First, we're going to collect old clothes.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory word.","explanation_ar":"فاصلة بعد الكلمة الاستهلالية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A team meeting around a table with a big chart titled with a heart icon: boxes of donated books, a calendar, and students raising hands to offer help. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A team meeting around a table with a big chart titled with a heart icon: boxes of donated books, a calendar, and students raising hands to offer help"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Helping Others”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Helping Others”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS5-T1","script":"We're going to collect books for the children's hospital. First, we're going to put posters around the school. Next, we're going to put boxes in every classroom. Omar said, \"I'll collect the boxes every day,\" and Adam promised, \"I won't forget to count the books.\" Finally, we're going to reuse old cardboard to make bookmarks. I think the children will be very happy with their new books!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Kindness Project: Language in Use”. Let’s learn will vs going to, community words with re-/un-, commas after introductory words (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Kindness meeting: in teams, choose a project (book drive, park clean-up, visiting the elderly). Each person makes an offer with \"I'll…\". The team agrees on 3 plans with \"We're going to…\" and makes one prediction with \"I think … will…\". Today you use all of Unit 2: will (offers, promises, opinions), going to (plans, evidence), community words, re-/un- and commas after introductory words. A project plan says what you are going to do, who will help, and what you think will happen. Here are some examples. We're going to clean the beach on Friday. First, we're going to buy gloves. I'll bring trash bags. Be careful! Some learners say: “First we will going to collect books.” That’s not right. We say: “First, we're going to collect books.” Plan → going to; comma after First. Quick check: what is wrong with “\"Who can help?\" – \"I'm going to help!\"”? … Think! … It should be “\"I'll help!\"”. Great job! Now you can say: I can plan a kindness project with my team.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Your hands are full. I ___ open the door for you.","options":["will to","'ll","opening","am going"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"Offer: I'll + base verb.","explanation_ar":"العرض: I'll + الفعل."},{"q":"I promise I ___ be late again.","options":["will not to","won't","don't","am not"],"answer":"won't","explanation":"Promise: I'll / I won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"الوعد بـ will أو won't."},{"q":"I think our school ___ win the competition.","options":["is","will to","will","wills"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."},{"q":"","options":["Grandpa will tells us a story tonight.","Grandpa will tell us a story tonight.","Grandpa will to tell us a story tonight.","Grandpa wills tell us a story tonight."],"answer":"Grandpa will tell us a story tonight.","explanation":"will + base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"will + الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"","options":["It doesn't will be easy, but we'll try.","It won't be easy, but we'll try.","It won't is easy, but we'll try.","It willn't be easy, but we'll try."],"answer":"It won't be easy, but we'll try.","explanation":"will not = won't.","explanation_ar":"won't تعني will not."},{"q":"\"Someone is at the door.\" – \"I ___ get it.\"","options":["'m going to have","getting","'ll","going to"],"answer":"'ll","explanation":"A decision now, an offer or a promise → will.","explanation_ar":"القرار اللحظي أو العرض ← will."},{"q":"We ___ plant trees on Saturday. We bought them yesterday.","options":["'re going to","going","wills","'ll to"],"answer":"'re going to","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"Look at that dog! It ___ eat your sandwich!","options":["will to","wills","going","'s going to"],"answer":"'s going to","explanation":"Prediction with evidence (Look!) → going to.","explanation_ar":"التوقع بدليل ← going to."},{"q":"Which one is an opinion about the future?","options":["\"We're going to travel on Monday.\"","\"I'm going to study tonight; I planned it.\"","\"I think it will be a great day.\"","\"Look! It's going to fall.\""],"answer":"\"I think it will be a great day.\"","explanation":"Prediction as an opinion (I think) → will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع كرأي ← will."},{"q":"Find the sentence that shows a plan made before.","options":["\"I'll help!\"","\"OK, I'll donate it!\"","\"I think he will donate it.\"","\"I'm going to donate my old bike next week.\""],"answer":"\"I'm going to donate my old bike next week.\"","explanation":"A plan decided before → be going to.","explanation_ar":"الخطة السابقة ← going to."},{"q":"un + kind = ___","options":["kindun","rekind","diskind","unkind"],"answer":"unkind","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"re + fill = ___","options":["fillre","overfill","refill","unfill"],"answer":"refill","explanation":"re- = again.","explanation_ar":"re تعني «مرة أخرى»."},{"q":"Our ___ helps us when we need him. He lives next door.","options":["volunteer","donation","charity","neighbor"],"answer":"neighbor","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"We should be kind to ___ people. (polite word for old)","options":["elderly","oldy","aged-up","olden"],"answer":"elderly","explanation":"elderly is a polite word for old people.","explanation_ar":"elderly كلمة مهذبة."},{"q":"The students ___ money for the charity.","options":["donated","unkind","rebuilt","volunteers"],"answer":"donated","explanation":"Choose the community word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"It's ___ to cross the road without looking.","options":["safety","safely","unsafe","resafe"],"answer":"unsafe","explanation":"un- = not / the opposite.","explanation_ar":"un تعني «غير»."},{"q":"","options":["First, we put on our gloves.","First we put on, our gloves.",", First we put on our gloves.","First we, put on our gloves."],"answer":"First, we put on our gloves.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Yes we will, help at the fair.","Yes, we, will help at the fair.","Yes we will help at the fair.","Yes, we will help at the fair."],"answer":"Yes, we will help at the fair.","explanation":"Yes / No / Well at the start of an answer → comma.","explanation_ar":"Yes وNo في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["However, the fair was a success.","However, the fair, was a success.","However the fair, was a success.","However the fair was a success."],"answer":"However, the fair was a success.","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We, finally, finished the project.","We, finally finished the project.","We finally finished the project.","We finally, finished the project."],"answer":"We finally finished the project.","explanation":"Don't add extra commas.","explanation_ar":"لا تضع فواصل زائدة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"Luckily the rain stopped.\"","options":["after \"Luckily\"","after \"rain\"","after \"the\"","after \"stopped\""],"answer":"after \"Luckily\"","explanation":"However / Also / Luckily at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"However في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a volunteer report:","options":["First we collected the trash next we recycled the bottles.","First, we collected the trash. Next, we recycled the bottles.","First we, collected the trash. Next, we recycled, the bottles.","First, we collected, the trash. Next we, recycled the bottles."],"answer":"First, we collected the trash. Next, we recycled the bottles.","explanation":"Sequence word at the start → comma.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التسلسل في البداية ← فاصلة."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i will to help you\"","options":["I wills help you.","i will help you.","I will to help you.","I will help you."],"answer":"I will help you.","explanation":"will + base verb (no -s, no to).","explanation_ar":"will + الفعل الأصلي."},{"q":"Will you help at the charity on Friday? – ___","options":["Yes, I'll.","Yes, I will.","Yes, I going to.","Yes, I wills."],"answer":"Yes, I will.","explanation":"Prediction or opinion: (I think) + will.","explanation_ar":"التوقع: I think + will."}],"theme_ar":"مساعدة الآخرين","essential_question_ar":"كيف يمكن للشباب أن يجعلوا مجتمعهم أفضل؟","can_do":"I can make offers, promises and predictions with will, and choose between will and going to.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أقدّم عروضًا ووعودًا وتوقعات باستخدام will، وأختار بين will وgoing to."});
